    "宋代斗茶尚黑釉建盏：“茶色白，宜黑盏”。碾末注汤，以茶筅回环击拂七汤，使雪白茶沫紧咬盏沿久聚不散（谓之“咬盏”），更可以清水幻化出竹石花鸟，称“水丹青（茶百戏": "Song tea contests prized black Jian bowls: 'White tea suits a black bowl.' Ground tea is whisked in seven pours so snow-white foam clings to the rim ('biting the bowl'), and water draws bamboo, stone, and birds ('tea pictorial art').",
